{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2020 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "1e3d7a2ce3c410e6b31e498c8f63e7b6d946ec2c1aeeb78b34f00ec338e58491" :edb/db-before-t 2019 :edb/db-after-t 2020 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535332 50 #inst "2026-10-08T22:17:53.481Z" 13194139535332 true] [17592186344236 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344237 13194139535332 false] [17592186344236 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344278 13194139535332 true] [17592186344236 1100 "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nis defined over the type I region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{2}y\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le 4-x-y}.\n$$\n\nUse $[a,b]$ as the full nonempty projection of the exactly specified region $R$ onto the $y$ axis. The inner limits may be piecewise. What is $a+b?$" 13194139535332 true] [17592186344236 1100 "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nis defined over the type I region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{2}y\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le 4-x-y}.\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b?$" 13194139535332 false] [17592186344236 1145 "A type I region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(x,y)\\le z\\le {u}_{2}(x,y)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type I region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/assets/1bd4b6d0b1aa955921c1f7855d3fbd95417072a67504d9de9be44dfbbed592e5.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type I region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,y)}^{{u}_{2}(x,y)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(x,y)=0,\\,{u}_{2}(x,y)=4-x-y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-y}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dA.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{2}y\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-y}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{y/2}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-y}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dx\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{y/2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-y}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=1+4=5.\n$$" 13194139535332 false] [17592186344236 1145 "The inequalities defining $R$ are retained exactly. A fiber is nonempty only when $x\\le4-y$. Combining this with $x\\ge y/2$ gives $y/2\\le4-y$, hence $y\\le8/3$. Every $y\\in[1,8/3]$ is attained, for example at $x=y/2$, $z=0$. Therefore the full nonempty projection is $[a,b]=[1,8/3]$ and\n\n$$a+b=1+\\frac83=\\frac{11}{3}.$$\n\nThe actual base is $D=\\{(x,y):1\\le y\\le8/3,\\ y/2\\le x\\le\\min(2,4-y)\\}$. The upper $x$ bounds meet at $y=2$, so the triple integral is\n\n$$\\iiint_R f\\,dV=\\int_1^2\\int_{y/2}^2\\int_0^{4-x-y}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy+\\int_2^{8/3}\\int_{y/2}^{4-y}\\int_0^{4-x-y}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy.$$\n\nFor $f=1$, these terms are $35/24$ and $1/9$, giving volume $113/72$. Using the printed nominal limits $1\\le y\\le4$ and $y/2\\le x\\le2$ instead includes reversed $z$ bounds. That formal signed integral gives $9/8$ and does not integrate over $R$. The source accepted the printed-endpoint sum $5$; the corrected study question asks for the full actual projection and adds $11/3$ as the correct choice." 13194139535332 true] [17592186344278 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344238 13194139535332 true] [17592186344278 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344239 13194139535332 true] [17592186344278 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344240 13194139535332 true] [17592186344278 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344241 13194139535332 true] [17592186344278 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344242 13194139535332 true] [17592186344278 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344279 13194139535332 true] [17592186344278 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535332 true] [17592186344278 1041 "selection" 13194139535332 true] [17592186344278 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344279 13194139535332 true] [17592186344278 1110 #uuid "8212b04b-1b2e-51a7-b8e6-54f518b38a70" 13194139535332 true] [17592186344279 1034 "\\frac{11}{3}" 13194139535332 true] [17592186344279 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535332 true] [17592186344279 1111 #uuid "32e657ea-6ba6-53f5-a5c8-44d39de51533" 13194139535332 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-161496/actual-projection-v1/selection" 17592186344278 "q-161496/actual-projection-v1/selection/answer-11-3" 17592186344279}}
